================================================================================
THE DATA IS NOT THE CODE
================================================================================

The MIT licence above covers the SOFTWARE in this repository — CandidateMapper.html,
everything in scripts/, and the documentation.

It does NOT and cannot relicense the third-party DATA the app fetches at runtime or
that the builders write into data/. That data arrives under its own terms, and some
of those terms carry obligations that survive redistribution. SOURCES.md is the full
audit; the three that matter most:

  · OpenStreetMap (ODbL 1.0) — data/transit.json, hospitals.json, theaters.json,
    fun.json, the world_poi OSM fallback, and any building geometry are Derivative
    Databases under ODbL. They must carry "© OpenStreetMap contributors" and, if
    redistributed, be offered under ODbL. This obligation attaches to those FILES,
    not to the code that reads them.

  · Wikipedia text (CC BY-SA 4.0) — summaries and descriptions shown in-app.
    Wikidata, by contrast, is CC0 and carries no obligation; prefer it where both
    sources carry the same fact.

  · Esri World Imagery, CARTO basemaps, Mapzen/Tilezen terrain — free to use with
    attribution, but proprietary or attribution-bound. Credit is rendered in the
    globe's corner; do not remove it.

Anyone redistributing a build of this app inherits those obligations. Anyone
redistributing only the source code in this repository does not.
